  "scientific_limits": {
    "en": "Entire Jurassic horseshoe crab based on SMNS65410, Kimmeridgian Nusplingen, not isolated shell or fossil slab. {\"units\": \"meters\", \"prosoma_width_published\": 0.104, \"prosoma_median_length_estimated\": 0.055, \"prosoma_genal_extent_estimated\": 0.08, \"thoracetron_length_estimated\": 0.045, \"thoracetron_width_estimated\": 0.07, \"telson_length_estimated\": 0.08, \"overall_length_estimated\": 0.18, \"dome_height_inferred\": 0.025, \"note\": \"Only104mm prosomalwidth directly published for SMNS65410. Other dimensions roughsameFig1A proportional estimates +/-15percent, not caliperdata. Shellmedianlength excludes longgenalposteriorpoints; bodytotalincludes telson.\"} SMNS65410 actual photograph and104mmwidth primary.2012/2020 other-specimen photos used for same-species outlinecomparison only, no covertmeasuretransfer. Briggs2005 fig1B/C andfig2 show exposed/decayed internalmuscles andgut; these are not living exterior decoration. Trace marks on surrounding substrate are not bodyparts. Wholelivingheight, missingleft/right limbpositions, terminaldetails, conservativeventralcovers, pose and mutedcolor are inferred; sex andadultstage notdetermined. AtlasFig34A-L same M.walchi; neighboringFig33/35 differenttaxa excluded.",
    "zh": "原创低多边形研究；形态、尺度及不确定性严格以本次已核参考为界。原始限定：Entire Jurassic horseshoe crab based on SMNS65410, Kimmeridgian Nusplingen, not isolated shell or fossil slab. {\"units\": \"meters\", \"prosoma_width_published\": 0.104, \"prosoma_median_length_estimated\": 0.055, \"prosoma_genal_extent_estimated\": 0.08, \"thoracetron_length_estimated\": 0.045, \"thoracetron_width_estimated\": 0.07, \"telson_length_estimated\": 0.08, \"overall_length_estimated\": 0.18, \"dome_height_inferred\": 0.025, \"note\": \"Only104mm prosomalwidth directly published for SMNS65410. Other dimensions roughsameFig1A proportional estimates +/-15percent, not caliperdata. Shellmedianlength excludes longgenalposteriorpoints; bodytotalincludes telson.\"} SMNS65410 actual photograph and104mmwidth primary.2012/2020 other-specimen photos used for same-species outlinecomparison only, no covertmeasuretransfer. Briggs2005 fig1B/C andfig2 show exposed/decayed internalmuscles andgut; these are not living exterior decoration. Trace marks on surrounding substrate are not bodyparts. Wholelivingheight, missingleft/right limbpositions, terminaldetails, conservativeventralcovers, pose and mutedcolor are inferred; sex andadultstage notdetermined. AtlasFig34A-L same M.walchi; neighboringFig33/35 differenttaxa excluded."
  },
